<% content_for :title, "Why Trello?" %>

<div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 py-8">
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">Why This App?</h1>

  <div class="prose prose-gray max-w-none text-sm text-gray-600 space-y-4">
    <p>
      I built this because I wanted a simple, self-hosted task manager. No subscriptions, no data leaving my machine, no bloated UI.
    </p>

    <p>
      Most project management tools are either too complex or too expensive. This is a minimal alternative that does one thing well: organize tasks into boards, lists, and cards.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800">Philosophy</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
      <li><strong>Simple</strong> — One hierarchy: Board → List → Card</li>
      <li><strong>Fast</strong> — Rails 8 with SQLite, no external dependencies</li>
      <li><strong>Local</strong> — Your data stays on your machine</li>
      <li><strong>Open</strong> — Full source on GitHub, MIT license</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800">Tech Stack</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
      <li>Ruby on Rails 8.1</li>
      <li>SQLite</li>
      <li>Tailwind CSS</li>
      <li>Stimulus + SortableJS</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>